WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:10.834
Russia has already started a new

00:00:10.967 --> 00:00:12.235
offensive in Ukraine.

00:00:12.368 --> 00:00:13.069
Ukrainian officials are already

00:00:13.203 --> 00:00:15.271
seeing a high tempo of Russian

00:00:15.405 --> 00:00:16.773
attacks, what they fear is a

00:00:16.906 --> 00:00:18.641
prelude to a massive new

00:00:18.775 --> 00:00:19.008
assault.

00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:21.411
&gt;&gt; One Ukrainian official says

00:00:21.544 --> 00:00:22.278
there was record shelling in the

00:00:22.412 --> 00:00:24.013
east this weekend, but these

00:00:24.013 --> 00:00:26.416
drone videos also show heavy

00:00:26.549 --> 00:00:29.419
losses for Ukrainian tanks.

00:00:29.552 --> 00:00:31.187
CNN's David Mckenzie is in

00:00:31.321 --> 00:00:32.222
Ukraine.

00:00:32.355 --> 00:00:34.023
David, does Ukraine believe a

00:00:34.023 --> 00:00:35.592
new Russian offensive has begun,

00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:37.393
it's under way now?

00:00:37.527 --> 00:00:38.962
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Victor, you can't

00:00:39.095 --> 00:00:40.363
really set your watch to it.

00:00:40.497 --> 00:00:44.033
What you have seen is this very

00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:46.035
significant uptick of attacks in

00:00:46.035 --> 00:00:47.504
certain parts of the eastern

00:00:47.637 --> 00:00:48.238
front.

00:00:48.371 --> 00:00:50.073
According to the nato

00:00:50.206 --> 00:00:51.307
secretary-general at least, he

00:00:51.441 --> 00:00:55.178
believes this has already

00:00:55.311 --> 00:00:58.815
started.

00:00:58.948 --> 00:01:01.651
&gt;&gt; We've seen it start already.

00:01:02.051 --> 00:01:04.254
We see what Russia will do now

00:01:04.387 --> 00:01:06.556
is send in thousands and

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:08.558
thousands of more troops,

00:01:08.691 --> 00:01:11.628
accepting a very high rate of

00:01:12.061 --> 00:01:14.130
casualty, taking big losses, but

00:01:14.264 --> 00:01:18.368
putting pressure on the

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:18.868
Ukrainians.

00:01:19.002 --> 00:01:21.271
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The pressure is

00:01:21.404 --> 00:01:23.573
being felt mostly around that

00:01:23.706 --> 00:01:32.081
eastern front, around vuhledar

00:01:32.115 --> 00:01:34.484
where you see Russian troops in

00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:37.053
wave after wave and getting

00:01:37.186 --> 00:01:38.388
obliterated by Ukrainian forces,

00:01:38.521 --> 00:01:40.156
at least based on the evidence

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.357
we've reviewed.

00:01:41.491 --> 00:01:44.093
They've been hitting minefields,

00:01:44.193 --> 00:01:49.599
attacked by drones and

00:01:49.732 --> 00:01:50.099
artillery.

00:01:50.099 --> 00:01:52.268
Even the Russian supporters are

00:01:52.402 --> 00:01:53.703
criticizing the Russians for

00:01:54.103 --> 00:01:55.371
throwing a huge amount of

00:01:55.505 --> 00:01:56.239
resources without much gain.

00:01:56.372 --> 00:02:00.476
One of the biggest issues with

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:02.111
the Ukraine space is they're

00:02:02.111 --> 00:02:04.113
running short of basic large

00:02:04.113 --> 00:02:05.048
caliber ammunition.

00:02:05.181 --> 00:02:06.816
That's something nato will be

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.117
discussing into tomorrow to try

00:02:08.151 --> 00:02:09.719
and ratchet up production to get

00:02:10.119 --> 00:02:12.121
them to the front.

00:02:12.121 --> 00:02:13.556
&gt;&gt; The delivery time to deliver

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.592
that ammunition is actually

00:02:15.725 --> 00:02:18.127
increasing we heard from

00:02:18.127 --> 00:02:20.129
Stoltenberg to 28 months from 12

00:02:20.229 --> 00:02:20.697
months.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.434
Quickly, David, there are

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:25.301
conflicting reports as to

00:02:25.435 --> 00:02:32.742
whether Russia is gaining

00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:33.109
traction.

00:02:33.242 --> 00:02:34.143
From what ou're seeing, is this

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.145
a formidable, reconstitutioned

00:02:36.145 --> 00:02:36.579
Russian force?

00:02:36.713 --> 00:02:38.982
&gt;&gt; Bianna, it's certainly too

00:02:39.115 --> 00:02:39.782
area to tell.

00:02:40.149 --> 00:02:44.320
In the areas of bakhmut, it's

00:02:44.454 --> 00:02:45.555
strategically important.

00:02:45.688 --> 00:02:49.726
If you look at this sent out by

00:02:50.159 --> 00:02:52.228
the Wagner mercenary group, it

00:02:52.362 --> 00:02:56.299
shows Wagner in place in what

00:02:56.432 --> 00:02:57.500
are significant parts of that

00:02:57.634 --> 00:02:59.636
satellite village, of that area.

00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:01.371
The Russians say they've largely

00:03:01.504 --> 00:03:03.706
taken control of this zone.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.974
The Ukrainians dispute that.

00:03:05.108 --> 00:03:06.843
Our teams on the ground are

00:03:06.976 --> 00:03:08.878
seeing that the entrances and

00:03:09.012 --> 00:03:12.315
exits of these towns are under

00:03:12.448 --> 00:03:14.817
Russia fire, which means for all

00:03:14.951 --> 00:03:16.185
intents and purposes, they do

00:03:16.185 --> 00:03:18.254
not have full control anymore of

00:03:18.388 --> 00:03:19.389
that zone.

00:03:19.522 --> 00:03:20.356
I remember being here several

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.191
months ago and speaking about

00:03:22.191 --> 00:03:24.394
the same towns and villages that

00:03:24.527 --> 00:03:28.965
were under constant bombardment

00:03:29.098 --> 00:03:29.265
then.

00:03:29.399 --> 00:03:32.568
So whether this attritional

00:03:32.702 --> 00:03:34.203
warfare brings any closer the

00:03:34.203 --> 00:03:35.738
aims of the Kremlin to take over

00:03:35.872 --> 00:03:37.473
those areas in the east, it

00:03:37.607 --> 00:03:38.941
certainly doesn't seem like it.

00:03:39.075 --> 00:03:43.112
This is very, very intense

00:03:43.246 --> 00:03:45.815
fighting, and neither side can

00:03:46.215 --> 00:03:46.616
potentially hold out forever

00:03:46.749 --> 00:03:48.751
with this kind of warfare.

00:03:48.885 --> 00:03:51.154
&gt;&gt; David Mckenzie, thank you.

00:03:51.287 --> 00:03:54.957
&gt;&gt;&gt; Retired U.S. Army major Mike

00:03:55.091 --> 00:03:56.225
Lyons joins us now.

00:03:56.292 --> 00:03:57.527
Let's pick up with the claim

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:01.731
from this Wagner group claiming

00:04:01.864 --> 00:04:03.099
control of back mud.

00:04:03.232 --> 00:04:05.201
It's not just the ability to

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:06.569
take over the village, but the

00:04:06.703 --> 00:04:07.470
ability to hold it.

00:04:07.603 --> 00:04:11.541
Do you think the Russian forces

00:04:11.674 --> 00:04:13.142
are better equipped this time

00:04:13.276 --> 00:04:14.510
around to hold this territory

00:04:14.644 --> 00:04:16.245
throughout the rest of the

00:04:16.245 --> 00:04:18.948
winter into the spring offensive

00:04:19.082 --> 00:04:20.516
it's expecting?

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.152
&gt;&gt; Victor, it's going to depend

00:04:23.286 --> 00:04:25.621
on how many reenforcements that

00:04:25.755 --> 00:04:29.192
Russians can get into the town

00:04:29.325 --> 00:04:30.660
and whether they decide to go on

00:04:30.793 --> 00:04:32.261
a full offensive.

00:04:32.261 --> 00:04:34.430
If they did, they would bypass

00:04:34.564 --> 00:04:35.898
that and not just look to stay

00:04:36.265 --> 00:04:37.066
there and hold it.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.367
What I see happening right now

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:40.436
from a military perspective is a

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:41.704
covering force battle.

00:04:41.838 --> 00:04:43.239
That happens right before the

00:04:43.372 --> 00:04:45.775
primary larger offensive scale

00:04:45.908 --> 00:04:46.275
operations.

00:04:46.375 --> 00:04:47.577
Reports I've seen show them

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:49.812
fighting along a front of about

00:04:49.946 --> 00:04:52.415
500, 600 kilometers, very wide

00:04:52.548 --> 00:04:54.283
there in the east.

00:04:54.417 --> 00:04:55.785
Again, it's not giving the

00:04:55.918 --> 00:04:59.722
Russians enough time to

00:04:59.856 --> 00:05:00.456
reenforce with certain soldiers

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:01.624
as they planned on doing.

00:05:01.758 --> 00:05:03.793
Ukraine is doing a very

00:05:03.926 --> 00:05:07.463
incredible job using artillery

00:05:07.597 --> 00:05:08.631
to fight back, as you saw,

00:05:08.765 --> 00:05:10.600
attacking some of the Russian

00:05:10.733 --> 00:05:11.267
soldiers in the open.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.503
&gt;&gt; The casualty rate, as you

00:05:13.636 --> 00:05:15.571
know, on both sides is extremely

00:05:15.705 --> 00:05:15.872
high.

00:05:16.305 --> 00:05:17.440
We don't know specific numbers.

00:05:17.573 --> 00:05:20.877
They've been pretty opaque from

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:25.481
Ukraine and perhaps that's

00:05:25.615 --> 00:05:25.948
understandable.

00:05:26.315 --> 00:05:30.319
But how should they approach in

00:05:30.319 --> 00:05:31.721
the early days of the offensive?

00:05:31.854 --> 00:05:33.156
&gt;&gt; We have to be very concerned

00:05:33.289 --> 00:05:34.357
that the equipment can't get

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:34.991
there on time.

00:05:35.124 --> 00:05:37.193
We don't see tanks showing up

00:05:37.326 --> 00:05:37.493
there.

00:05:37.627 --> 00:05:39.128
There are certain videos you see

00:05:39.262 --> 00:05:40.363
on the internet.

00:05:40.496 --> 00:05:43.132
But they're howitzers and the

00:05:43.266 --> 00:05:43.833
like.

00:05:43.966 --> 00:05:45.368
Also, the ammunition, that in

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:48.371
and of itself is a tremendous

00:05:48.504 --> 00:05:48.838
problem.

00:05:48.971 --> 00:05:50.907
As the secretary-general said,

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.341
if nato countries don't start

00:05:52.475 --> 00:05:54.343
mobilizing more artillery

00:05:54.443 --> 00:05:55.511
rounds, it looks like Ukraine

00:05:55.645 --> 00:05:57.213
runs out of ammunition in the

00:05:57.346 --> 00:05:58.881
next few months given the amount

00:05:59.015 --> 00:06:01.450
of artillery the Russians are

00:06:01.584 --> 00:06:02.485
firing at them.

00:06:02.618 --> 00:06:04.353
&gt;&gt; We heard from

00:06:04.353 --> 00:06:05.188
secretary-general Stoltenberg

00:06:05.321 --> 00:06:08.357
that, for example, the

00:06:08.457 --> 00:06:09.325
large-caliber ammunition

00:06:09.458 --> 00:06:14.363
increase Friday a 12 to 28-month

00:06:14.363 --> 00:06:16.432
order placed to delivery time.

00:06:16.566 --> 00:06:18.434
Something ordered today would be

00:06:18.568 --> 00:06:19.735
delivered almost two and a half

00:06:19.869 --> 00:06:20.703
years out.

00:06:20.837 --> 00:06:22.371
Will there come a point at which

00:06:22.371 --> 00:06:24.373
the allies will say no, we

00:06:24.373 --> 00:06:25.842
simply cannot give you more

00:06:25.975 --> 00:06:28.744
because we don't have it to

00:06:28.878 --> 00:06:30.947
give?

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:31.614
&gt;&gt; I think that's going to

00:06:31.747 --> 00:06:33.082
depend on how well the Ukraine

00:06:33.216 --> 00:06:35.518
military does over the next 90

00:06:35.651 --> 00:06:35.818
days.

00:06:35.952 --> 00:06:38.721
If the Ukraine military can

00:06:38.855 --> 00:06:39.956
actually threaten Russian

00:06:40.389 --> 00:06:41.357
troops, maybe more in the south,

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:42.592
maybe threaten crimea.

00:06:42.725 --> 00:06:44.060
If they can do that and show

00:06:44.393 --> 00:06:45.661
they're making advances and at

00:06:45.795 --> 00:06:47.530
least get to a hard stalemate on

00:06:47.663 --> 00:06:49.899
the ground, then maybe they

00:06:50.032 --> 00:06:50.399
negotiate.

00:06:50.399 --> 00:06:51.868
The position they have is still

00:06:52.001 --> 00:06:54.003
not what they want because

00:06:54.403 --> 00:06:55.538
they've still given up some land

00:06:55.671 --> 00:06:56.405
to Russia.

00:06:56.839 --> 00:06:59.275
I think it's going to determine

00:06:59.408 --> 00:07:00.409
how well they fight.

00:07:00.409 --> 00:07:01.811
If they get Russia to the

00:07:01.944 --> 00:07:02.979
negotiating table, it's going to

00:07:03.112 --> 00:07:05.748
be a potentially long haul,

00:07:05.882 --> 00:07:06.482
though.

00:07:06.616 --> 00:07:07.817
We'll have to industrialize some

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:09.452
of our industries in order to

00:07:09.585 --> 00:07:11.754
make sure we can meet that

00:07:11.888 --> 00:07:12.421
requirement.

00:07:12.488 --> 00:07:13.356
It's definitely excessive.

00:07:13.489 --> 00:07:14.557
&gt;&gt; There's no indication that

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:15.591
Vladimir Putin is serious about

00:07:15.725 --> 00:07:17.994
getting back to the negotiating

00:07:18.427 --> 00:07:18.861
table any time soon.

00:07:18.995 --> 00:07:20.062
We know Ukrainians continue to

00:07:20.429 --> 00:07:22.431
ask for longer-range weapons.

00:07:22.431 --> 00:07:24.433
Thus far the United States says

00:07:24.433 --> 00:07:24.867
no.

00:07:25.001 --> 00:07:27.603
There's a "Washington post"

00:07:27.737 --> 00:07:29.105
report that says that Ukrainian

00:07:29.238 --> 00:07:30.940
officials have only launched

00:07:31.073 --> 00:07:33.776
these long-range, more advanced

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:36.612
weapons, the himarches in

00:07:36.746 --> 00:07:37.947
particular with coordination

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.048
from the United States.

00:07:39.181 --> 00:07:41.417
Do you think hearing that is a

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:42.451
sign from Ukrainians that

00:07:42.551 --> 00:07:44.453
perhaps they can be trusted with

00:07:44.587 --> 00:07:45.955
these longer-range weapon and

00:07:46.088 --> 00:07:47.256
won't be directed into the

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:50.559
Russian Federation itself?

00:07:50.693 --> 00:07:53.362
&gt;&gt; The himars are giving the

00:07:53.496 --> 00:07:54.563
Ukraine military an advantage in

00:07:54.697 --> 00:07:56.832
what was in the past mass fire

00:07:56.966 --> 00:07:58.634
weapon, destroying wide swaths

00:07:58.768 --> 00:08:00.469
of land in areas.

00:08:00.469 --> 00:08:01.938
Now they can be much more

00:08:02.071 --> 00:08:02.471
precise.

00:08:02.471 --> 00:08:04.473
But the longer-range artillery

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.709
fire and missiles and rockets is

00:08:06.842 --> 00:08:07.376
what Ukraine wants.

00:08:07.610 --> 00:08:09.312
I think there's a real risk for

00:08:09.445 --> 00:08:10.479
the United States government to

00:08:10.479 --> 00:08:11.981
do that as those become truly

00:08:12.114 --> 00:08:12.682
offensive weapons.

00:08:12.815 --> 00:08:14.483
They could be launched into the

00:08:14.617 --> 00:08:14.750
sea.

00:08:14.884 --> 00:08:16.485
They could be launched over the

00:08:16.585 --> 00:08:17.420
border into Russia.

00:08:17.553 --> 00:08:19.388
I think that's where the slope

00:08:19.522 --> 00:08:20.856
becomes slippery where, if

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:22.491
Ukraine wants to decide they

00:08:22.591 --> 00:08:27.863
want to do that for their own

00:08:27.997 --> 00:08:28.531
survivability, once we give

00:08:28.664 --> 00:08:29.398
those weapons to them, we can't

00:08:29.532 --> 00:08:30.499
get it back.

00:08:30.499 --> 00:08:31.334
I don't know that it's a matter

00:08:31.467 --> 00:08:34.637
of trust, but the type of

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:35.771
warfare for those weapons,

00:08:35.905 --> 00:08:37.273
they're purely offensive.

00:08:37.406 --> 00:08:38.674
&gt;&gt; You said we would have to.

00:08:39.141 --> 00:08:40.810
I wonder if we means the west,

00:08:40.943 --> 00:08:42.778
the allies of Ukraine, would

00:08:42.912 --> 00:08:44.013
have to industrialize some of

00:08:44.146 --> 00:08:46.882
our industry to provide

00:08:47.016 --> 00:08:47.516
ammunition to Ukraine.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:49.518
Are you talking about invoking

00:08:49.652 --> 00:08:51.354
defense production to pass that

00:08:51.487 --> 00:08:53.122
ammunition on to a third nation?

00:08:53.255 --> 00:08:54.991
Is that what you're saying, or

00:08:55.124 --> 00:08:56.525
am I getting that wrong?

00:08:56.525 --> 00:09:00.529
&gt;&gt; I'm talking about actually

00:09:00.529 --> 00:09:00.997
manufacturing.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:02.565
Talking to people in that

00:09:02.698 --> 00:09:05.301
industry, 155 artillery rounds

00:09:05.434 --> 00:09:08.004
consists of dynamite shells that

00:09:08.137 --> 00:09:13.542
are easy to manufacture.

00:09:13.676 --> 00:09:15.011
The fuses are mechanical timed

00:09:15.144 --> 00:09:17.046
fuses.

00:09:17.179 --> 00:09:17.747
The different components for

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.547
those to be manufactured takes

00:09:18.614 --> 00:09:18.781
time.

00:09:18.914 --> 00:09:19.982
We'd have to secure the raw

00:09:20.116 --> 00:09:21.650
materials to do that.

00:09:21.784 --> 00:09:24.653
The United States manufactures

00:09:24.787 --> 00:09:26.022
450,000 to 50,000 rounds for

00:09:26.155 --> 00:09:27.723
itself on a monthly basis.

00:09:27.857 --> 00:09:30.559
In order to help Ukraine, for

00:09:30.626 --> 00:09:31.560
example, other nat tow countries

00:09:31.694 --> 00:09:33.362
would have to supply about that

00:09:33.496 --> 00:09:35.898
or more on a monthly basis.

00:09:36.032 --> 00:09:37.733
We would then cut into our own

00:09:37.867 --> 00:09:38.834
stocks, and that's just

00:09:38.968 --> 00:09:40.569
something we're not going to do.

00:09:40.569 --> 00:09:41.971
We would have to increase our

00:09:42.104 --> 00:09:42.972
production of artillery rounds

00:09:43.105 --> 00:09:44.573
in particular in order to meet

00:09:44.573 --> 00:09:45.174
that objective.

